SUMMARY:JOHNNY ALLAIR
DESCRIPTION:Dinner and A Show with JOHNNY ALLAIR \nJohn Allair’s musical career began at the vanguard of early Rock & Roll and Rhythm & Blues in the San Francisco Bay Area in the 1950s – eventually leading him to tour the world as a long-time member of Van Morrison’s band. \nHe has recorded or crossed paths with John Lee Hooker\, Huey Lewis\, Elvin Bishop\, Maria Muldaur\, Tom Waits\, B.B. King\, Big Mama Thornton\, Lloyd Price\, Charlie Musselwhite\, Joan Baez\, Steve Miller\, Charles Brown\, Johnny Otis  Louie Belson\, Jimmy Witherspoon\, Bobby Freeman\, Memphis Slim\, John Handy\, Bonnie Raitt\, Sammy Hagar\, Dan Hicks\, Norton Buffalo\, Dr. John\, Little Willie Littlefield\, Tom Fogerty\, Nick Gravenites\, Chris Issak\, Taj Mahal\, Country Joe\, Boz Scaggs\, & Buddy Guy\, He sat in with Fats Domino’s band at the old Fillmore Auditorium in 1958\, and with Van Morrison opened for the Rolling Stones in 2006. He recently finished his latest tour and recordings with Van.
URL:https://ranchonicasio.com/event/johnny-allair-3/
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio\, 1 Old Rancheria Rd\, Nicasio\, CA\, 94946\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ranchonicasio.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Johnny-Allair-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
